{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:26:35.690Z","data":{"text":"The task is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**New file: `src/core/status/steering-change.ts`**\n- `findSteeringChange(projectRoot, config, id)` — active change first, else archived steered change in an osq worktree, else null.\n- `listArchivedSteering(projectRoot, config)` — every archived worktree change whose derived state has `steering`, in numeric order.\n- Both derive state in the change's own tree via `readChangeFolder(change.tree.root, change.folderPath)` and write nothing. Returns a `SteeringChange { change, state }`.\n\n**`src/core/status/next-step.ts`**\n- Archived changes now derive state: `dead` with `osq plan <id>` / `needs steering` when steering is present, otherwise `landed` as before.\n\n**`src/core/status/inbox-projection.ts`**\n- `readInbox` adds one `change-regressed` needs-you item per archived steering change (no task, `osq plan <id>`, first trigger as `steering`), merged and sorted by numeric change id. `inbox.ts`/`inbox-text.ts` untouched.\n\n**`src/core/status/dispatch-items.ts`**\n- Extracted `steeringHaltItem`; archived steering changes produce exactly one no-task `halt` item (`osq plan`/`osq show`, first trigger), and their `land` item is suppressed.\n\n**New test: `tests/steering-archived.test.ts`**\n- Copies task 2's temp-git-repo setup, archives two changes, lands the first against a conflicting default branch, and covers the \"Archived change found for steering\", \"Inbox row\", \"Change next step\", and \"Dispatch items\" scenarios.\n\nVerification: `node --import tsx --test tests/steering-archived.test.ts` passes (4/4), and the full `pnpm verify` chain completed through lint. Result written to `openspec/changes/129-default-branch-steering/.run/results/3.md`."}}
